<div class="button-view">
    <div id="stake-infos" class="stake-infos">

        <p class="descr">Unstake is used to get tokens back to the hands of a user. For that, received funds must be returned, to be claimable for future token holder</p>
        <p class="descr">If some tokens are staked, user got his funds in the past and in a meantime additional funds were added, tokens proportionate to "covering" additional funds can be unstaked, without returning any funds. </p>
        <p class="descr">Example:  total funds are 100, user stakes 10% of total allocation, receives 9(90% of 10% of total funds) funds. Later:total funds are 200, user can unstake 5% of total allocation without returning funds, since the remaining 5% is enough to cover funds already received</p>
        <P class="separator"></P>
        <p>Tokens you hold, you staked, GWEI you received </p>
        <p>
            <div id="balance-container" style="display: flex;">
            <span id="total-balance-u"></span>
            <span id="already-staked-u"></span>
            <span id="already-borrowed-u"></span>
        </div>
        </p>

        <p>Reevaluate all and return <span><input type="number" id="unstake-input" value="0" /></span> GWEI more</span></p>
        <p style="padding: 30px;">
            you will get
            <span id="unstake-amount-display"> </span> <span><%= tokenDetails.name %></span>
        </p>
        <p style="padding: 30px;">
            <a id="unstake-execute-button" href="#" class="button">let's do it</a>
        </p>
    </div>

</div>

<script src="scriptsUnstake.js"></script>
<script>
    // Create an object to store token details mapped to token addresses
    window.tokenDetails = {
        tokenAddress: '<%= tokenDetails.tokenAddress %>',
        registryAddress: '<%= tokenDetails.registryAddress %>',
        name: '<%= tokenDetails.name %>',
        decimals: '<%= tokenDetails.decimals %>',
        symbol: '<%= tokenDetails.symbol %>',
        decimals: '<%= tokenDetails.decimals %>',
        logoPath: '<%= tokenDetails.logoPath %>',
        totalFunds: '<%=  tokenDetails.totalFunds %>',
        totalSupply: '<%=  tokenDetails.totalSupply %>',
    }
</script>